From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] os_install_service: Gentoo's coreutils and lvm2 calls

NickelOS Unified runs Gentoo's coreutils and lvm2. chromeos-install's cp
made directories with mkdirat and set owners with fchownat, which this
policy killed ("Bad system call", the install failed after preloading the
DLCs); lvm2's pvs does its I/O through Linux AIO. Found by tracing a full
install outside the sandbox: these are all the calls it makes that the
policy didn't list.

---
--- a/conf/os_install_service-seccomp-amd64.policy
+++ b/conf/os_install_service-seccomp-amd64.policy
@@ -57,6 +57,8 @@
 fchdir: 1
 fchmod: 1
 fchown: 1
+# NickelOS Unified: Gentoo's coreutils (cp -a) sets owners with fchownat.
+fchownat: 1
 fcntl: 1
 fgetxattr: 1
 flistxattr: 1
@@ -86,6 +88,11 @@
 getuid: 1
 inotify_add_watch: 1
 inotify_init1: 1
+# NickelOS Unified: Gentoo's lvm2 does its I/O through Linux AIO (libaio).
+io_destroy: 1
+io_getevents: 1
+io_setup: 1
+io_submit: 1
 lchown: 1
 lgetxattr: 1
 linkat: 1
@@ -94,6 +101,8 @@
 lsetxattr: 1
 lstat: 1
 mkdir: 1
+# NickelOS Unified: Gentoo's coreutils (cp, mkdir) make directories with mkdirat.
+mkdirat: 1
 mmap: arg2 in ~PROT_EXEC || arg2 in ~PROT_WRITE
 madvise: arg2 == MADV_DONTNEED || arg2 == MADV_GUARD_INSTALL
 mseal: 1
